# and the 20-quality stat comparison through the stand-in calcFunc), gem 2 enabled (the toggle
# comparison) and gem 1 count (the note); edit gem 1 level (BACK, BACK, "15"), gem 2 quality (the
# + button twice); untick gem 3 (enabled changeFunc); delete gem 1 ("x": the rows below take its
# place); type "Fireball" + RETURN in the empty row (the gemChangeFunc creates the instance); gem
# 1 count "2"; type "zz" into gem 3 (Fireball) and click away (the gem selector's focus-lost path
# into the change function); then group 6 (Vaal Double Strike: the enableGlobal check boxes and
# the shifted rows), untick its enableGlobal1 and enableGlobal2. (No gem selector of a group with
# supports is focused or hovered: the LuaCalcBridge leaves `supportEffect.isSupporting` keyed by
# its own gem copies, so PoB's support highlight, GemSelectControl.lua:631-638, never shows on the
# Rust side; CCR-0119 §6.)
